Fix the crash of GTK 4.16 on compositors that expose linux-dmabuf v6.

The linux-dmabuf-unstable-v1 protocol deprecates the main_device event in
version 6: a compositor no longer sends it, and the client is expected to use
the tranche that carries the sampling flag instead. GDK 4.16 binds the
version that the compositor advertises, but its feedback handler still
allocates the pending format set from main_device, so the first
tranche_done event dereferences a NULL pointer and the application dies with
a SIGSEGV while Gtk.init() opens the display.

GTK 4.20 fixed this upstream by never binding above version 5, which keeps
the v5 semantics where main_device is always sent. This patch backports that
one-line change, so the bundled GTK behaves like a current one.

Upstream fix: gdk/wayland/gdkdisplay-wayland.c, bind with
MIN (version, LINUX_DMABUF_VERSION) where LINUX_DMABUF_VERSION is 5.

--- a/gdk/wayland/gdkdisplay-wayland.c
+++ b/gdk/wayland/gdkdisplay-wayland.c
@@ -96,6 +96,10 @@
 
 #define MIN_SYSTEM_BELL_DELAY_MS 20
 
+/* The linux-dmabuf v6 feedback no longer sends main_device, and this GDK only
+ * implements the v5 semantics, so bind no higher than v5. */
+#define LINUX_DMABUF_VERSION     5
+
 #define GTK_SHELL1_VERSION       5
 #define OUTPUT_VERSION_WITH_DONE 2
 #define NO_XDG_OUTPUT_DONE_SINCE_VERSION 3
@@ -370,7 +374,8 @@
       struct zwp_linux_dmabuf_feedback_v1 *feedback;
 
       display_wayland->linux_dmabuf =
-        wl_registry_bind (display_wayland->wl_registry, id, &zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1_interface, version);
+        wl_registry_bind (display_wayland->wl_registry, id, &zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1_interface,
+                          MIN (version, LINUX_DMABUF_VERSION));
       feedback = zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1_get_default_feedback (display_wayland->linux_dmabuf);
       display_wayland->dmabuf_formats_info = dmabuf_formats_info_new (GDK_DISPLAY (display_wayland),
                                                                       "default",
